@Technique::TrainingFreeLooped::[reproduce]

@Comment::[Paper: Training-Free Looped Transformers (Chen, Li, Liang, Lao, Liu 2026, arXiv:2605.23872v1, UT Austin). Inference-time wrapper that loops a contiguous mid-stack window [a,b] of a frozen checkpoint K times; pre-norm block = one forward Euler step on x' = F_g(x), so looping refines the SAME t=1 endpoint instead of integrating to t=K (Eq.6-10). Damped sub-steps, front-loaded RK tableau (Eq.13-16, Alg.1-3), block-mode vs layer-mode (Sec 2.2, Alg.4/5), snapshot/restore + stash KV protocol (Alg.4/5, Eq.19). Graded scope: main text + full appendix - Eq.9/10/16, App B.1/B.2 proofs, Table 1 strategy family, Fig.2/4/5, Tables 2/3/4/6/7/8/9/10/11/12/15/16/17/18/19/20/21, App Fig.6 depth rule, wall-clock + decode modes, block-vs-layer + MoE routing proxy, repo audit. Repo note: NO verifiable official code (paper PDF links only its own arXiv page; github.com/L-z-Chen/Training-Free-Looped-Transformer is 404 with no Wayback snapshot); derivation is paper-only, third-party repos used as non-authoritative cross-checks. Five paper-side discrepancies recorded.]

